{
  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile avgpool is currently the best single-modality result (0.6501 acc, 0.6275 F1), while the closest multimodal test, scvi_n200 + resnet50 with avgpool and concat fusion, is slightly lower (0.6315 acc, 0.6068 F1). The main uncertainty is whether the small multimodal gap is due to the image modality being weak or to the simple concat fusion being suboptimal. config_031 changes only the fusion method from concat to weighted while keeping the strongest RNA encoder, image encoder, profile setting, and aggregation fixed. This is a focused, low-risk extension of the best multimodal evidence and will clarify whether weighted fusion can make the multimodal model competitive with the RNA-only baseline before investing further in more complex multimodal variants."
}

